From 33f61259cd1a32ee15cc6971630af1bff0c091fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: openhands <openhands@all-hands.dev>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 15:52:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Modernize Forge Engine: blue sky, volumetric clouds, PBR,
 inspector, Unity camera/export

Rename DX12ForgeEngine -> ForgeEngine (class, CMake target, binary, project
marker, UI branding); legacy DX12FORGE_* scene/post-process tags still load.

Sky: single continuous elevation ramp (zenith->mid->horizon) plus Mie horizon
glow, so the dome reads vivid azure instead of collapsing to white under ACES +
gamma. Cumulus deck derives a density normal for bright tops / shadowed bases
and fades with distance (aerial perspective). Verified all HLSL entry points
compile with DXC and the simulated sky is blue in every direction.

PBR: emissive texture slot + emissive/occlusion constants, emission added after
lighting for bloom, authored AO strength honored, two-sided pipeline. Scene
format v8/v9 persist emissive map, normal scale, occlusion and double-sided.

Inspector/API: Add Component popup with Rendering submenu and per-object
hasMaterial gating; camera inspector (ortho, clip, depth, background, skybox,
gizmos, culling mask). C# Material and State-backed Camera classes, new Rotator/
Oscillator/KillBelowY/MaterialPulse components. Fixed an off-by-six field index
in the native SET parser that silently dropped script-driven camera edits.

Camera: Unity-style preview panel fed by the real post-processed frame; Look
Through Camera drives the Scene viewport. Export: data ships in a <Product>_Data
folder and CopyGameAssets skips engine source/build/host trees.

Verified: 9/9 HLSL entry points compile (DXC), ForgeEngine.API and
ForgeScriptHost build with 0 warnings/0 errors (.NET 8).

Co-authored-by: openhands <openhands@all-hands.dev>
